Extract one object per signoff person. If multiple people signed, create separate objects for each.

A "signoff person" is strictly defined as an individual who is executing, adopting, or authorizing the document itself (typically found in the main signature block or under clauses like "IN WITNESS WHEREOF", or preceded by a date/location line such as "Stuttgart im November 2025" or a company name line acting as a signature block introduction).

CRITICAL INSTRUCTION: Do NOT extract individuals who are merely listed, referenced, or authorized within the body of the document, exhibits, annexes, or schedules (e.g., authorized bank signatories, local signatories, etc.), unless they are also the ones executing the main agreement.

FIELDS TO EXTRACT:

1. NAME
   Extract the full name of each person who signed the main document.
   Source: Main signature block, printed name below the execution signature, or certified-by section.

2. DESIGNATION
   Extract the role/title of the signoff person (e.g., Director, Chairman of the Board of Management).
   Source: Look at the text immediately next to/below the signature line. If no title is present there, scan the document's preamble or introductory paragraphs. If their capacity can be clearly established from the document's context, extract that title. If it cannot be determined anywhere in the document, set "NA".

OUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE:
{
  "Signoff_Persons": [
    {
      "Name": "John Smith",
      "Designation": "Director"
    },
    {
      "Name": "Jane Doe",
      "Designation": "NA"
    }
  ]
}
